# Copy to .env and fill in. Holds the secrets that are kept out of
# config.json: the Cloudflare API token(s), and the router credentials for the
# WAN failover / CGNAT guard.
#
# Cloudflare: a zone or item without `apiKey` / `apiKeyEnv` in config.json uses
# CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN. `apiKeyEnv` names a different variable, for setups with
# one token per zone (e.g. CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN_OTHER below). A literal
# `apiKey` in config.json still works.
#
# The router credentials for the password-based transports (asuswrt-merlin
# `web`, routeros `rest`) are kept out of config.json: `usernameEnv` and
# `passwordEnv` name the variables to read them from, so the config file stays
# safe to share. The ssh transports use key auth and read neither; their user
# is `ssh.user` in config.json.
#
# `npm run start` and `npm run dev` load it. Running node directly, pass
# --env-file, which needs no dependency:
#   node --env-file-if-exists=./.env ./src/index.js
#
# Keep this file mode 0600. It is gitignored.

CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=
# CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN_OTHER=

ROUTER_USERNAME=
ROUTER_PASSWORD=
